        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 68-year-old male, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers consistent with infective exacerbation. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Clinical monitoring including pulse oximetry and repeated vital signs was maintained throughout. He responded well to treatment with clear symptomatic improvement. At discharge, he was stable with adequate oxygenation on room air. Please ensure continuation of his inhaler therapy and arrange outpatient pulmonary follow-up. Patient education regarding exacerbation recognition was provided prior to discharge.</div>"
            },
